# Reference conversation of the original MS1 firmware (application 4011) as M-CAN master with
# the same firmware as slave, run in the emulator ms1-emu: difftest runs both MS1s in one
# process, in lockstep, on one CAN bus. Frames as the master sees them: TX = sent by the MS1
# master, RX = sent by the MS1 slave. Columns as `ms1emu -c` writes them: time (s, emulated
# since reset), direction, 29-bit ID, [DLC], data. Both MS1s have the UID 000752E2 (same image).
#
# Captured with (EMPTY = an empty file; master.txt and slave.txt below):
#   difftest -W -t 38 -s master.txt -M ms1_4011.s19 -A 0=0 -S slave.txt -c ms1_reference.can \
#       ms1_4011.s19 ms1_4011.s19 EMPTY EMPTY
#
# master.txt (the master's operator): add loco 3 by address, release it, STOP, GO
#   12.0 press knob / 12.15 release knob / 13.0 turn 1 / 13.5 press knob / 13.65 release knob
#   14.5 turn 2 / 15.0 press knob / 15.15 release knob / 16.0 press knob / 16.15 release knob
#   17.0 press ok / 17.15 release ok / 28.0 press stop / 28.15 release stop
#   29.0 press stop / 29.15 release stop
# slave.txt (the slave's operator): take loco 3 (esc), speed up, light, F (pa0), speed down,
# direction (knob), speed, STOP, GO, light off, then the CAN cable pulled
#   18.0 press esc / 18.15 release esc / 19.0 turn 10 / 20.0 press light / 20.15 release light
#   21.0 press pa0 / 21.15 release pa0 / 22.0 turn -12 / 23.0 press knob / 23.15 release knob
#   24.0 turn 4 / 25.0 press stop / 25.15 release stop / 26.0 press stop / 26.15 release stop
#   27.0 press light / 27.15 release light / 31.0 unplug
#
# What happens: 9.34 s the master's CAN starts (8 x 0x380), the slave registers (node 1) and
# sets up with an empty lokstack; 16.0 the master adds loco 3 (object 0x200) and drives it
# itself, 17.0 releases it; 18.0 the slave takes it and drives it; 25-26 STOP/GO from the
# slave, 28-29 from the master; 31.0 the slave is unplugged, the master polls it every 256 ms
# and gives it up 5.116 s after its last frame (no frame after 35.83 s; the run ends at 38 s).
